1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,846
Woman:

2
00:00:01,846 --> 00:00:08,246
Jack, I’m thinking of taking the kids to the seaside on a surfing holiday this summer

3
00:00:08,246 --> 00:00:12,860
and I wanted to ask your advice – as I know you’re such an

4
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:12,910
expert.

5
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:13,161
Jack:

6
00:00:13,161 --> 00:00:15,365
Well, I don’t know about that,

7
00:00:15,365 --> 00:00:19,241
but yes, I’ve done a bit of surfing over the years.

8
00:00:19,241 --> 00:00:20,836
I’d thoroughly recommend it.

9
00:00:20,836 --> 00:00:25,302
I think it’s the kind of holiday all the family can enjoy together.

10
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:29,131
The thing about surfing is that it’s great for all ages

11
00:00:29,131 --> 00:00:30,088
and all abilities.

12
00:00:30,088 --> 00:00:32,640
My youngest started when he was only three!

13
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:33,026
Woman:

14
00:00:33,026 --> 00:00:33,413
Wow!

15
00:00:33,413 --> 00:00:36,892
But it’s quite physically demanding, isn’t it?

16
00:00:36,892 --> 00:00:40,370
I’ve heard you need to be pretty fit.

17
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:40,705
Jack:

18
00:00:40,705 --> 00:00:41,040
Yes.

19
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:45,060
You’ll certainly learn more quickly and won’t tire as easily.

20
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:45,392
Woman:

21
00:00:45,392 --> 00:00:47,716
Well – that should be OK for us.

22
00:00:47,716 --> 00:00:51,700
You’ve been surfing a few times in Ireland, haven’t you?

23
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:52,091
Jack:

24
00:00:52,091 --> 00:00:52,481
Yes.

25
00:00:52,481 --> 00:00:54,826
There’s some great surfing there,

26
00:00:54,826 --> 00:00:57,170
which people don’t always realise.

27
00:00:57,170 --> 00:00:57,556
Woman:

28
00:00:57,556 --> 00:00:59,870
And which locations would you recommend?

29
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:02,570
– there seem to be quite a few.

30
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:02,926
Jack:

31
00:01:02,926 --> 00:01:04,348
Yes, there are loads.

32
00:01:04,348 --> 00:01:06,836
Last year we went to County Donegal.

33
00:01:06,836 --> 00:01:09,680
There are several great places to surf there.

34
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:10,102
Woman:

35
00:01:10,102 --> 00:01:12,212
What about in County Clare?

36
00:01:12,212 --> 00:01:16,010
I read that’s also really good for surfing.

37
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:16,333
Jack:

38
00:01:16,333 --> 00:01:17,302
Yes, it is.

39
00:01:17,302 --> 00:01:19,563
I’ve been there a few times.

40
00:01:19,563 --> 00:01:21,178
Most people go to Lahinch.

41
00:01:21,178 --> 00:01:22,794
My kids love it there.

42
00:01:22,794 --> 00:01:26,670
The waves aren’t too challenging and the town is very lively.

43
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:27,090
Woman:

44
00:01:27,090 --> 00:01:29,190
Are there good hotels there?

45
00:01:29,190 --> 00:01:29,557
Jack:

46
00:01:29,557 --> 00:01:34,331
Yes – some very nice ones and there are also a few basic hostels

47
00:01:34,331 --> 00:01:35,066
and campsites.

48
00:01:35,066 --> 00:01:39,840
It’s great if you need lessons as the surf schools are excellent.

49
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:40,280
Woman:

50
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,160
Sounds good.

51
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:41,467
Jack:

52
00:01:41,467 --> 00:01:45,769
Yes and there’s lots to see in the area – like those well-known cliffs

53
00:01:45,769 --> 00:01:47,920
– … I’ve forgotten the name of them …

54
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:48,210
Woman:

55
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:50,820
Oh don’t worry – I can look them up.

56
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:51,162
Jack:

57
00:01:51,162 --> 00:01:53,895
I’ve also been surfing in County Mayo,

58
00:01:53,895 --> 00:01:55,945
which is less well-known for surfing,

59
00:01:55,945 --> 00:01:58,337
but we had a really good time.

60
00:01:58,337 --> 00:02:02,095
That was a few years ago when the kids were younger.

61
00:02:02,095 --> 00:02:05,170
There’s a good surf school at Carrowniskey beach.

62
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:05,430
Woman:

63
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:06,730
How do you spell that?

64
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:10,253
Jack:

65
00:02:10,253 --> 00:02:17,300
C-A-double R-O-W-N-I-S-K-E-Y

66
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:17,970
Woman:

67
00:02:17,970 --> 00:02:18,640
OK.

68
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:18,934
Jack:

69
00:02:18,934 --> 00:02:23,053
I put the kids into the surf camp they run during the summer for

70
00:02:23,053 --> 00:02:24,230
10–16 year olds.

71
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:24,640
Woman:

72
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:25,460
Oh right.

73
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:27,510
How long was that for?

74
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:27,863
Jack:

75
00:02:27,863 --> 00:02:30,337
Three hours every day for a week.

76
00:02:30,337 --> 00:02:33,870
It was perfect – they were so tired out after that.

77
00:02:33,870 --> 00:02:34,208
Woman:

78
00:02:34,208 --> 00:02:35,220
I can imagine.

79
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:35,546
Jack:

80
00:02:35,546 --> 00:02:40,103
One thing we did while the kids were surfing was to rent some kayaks

81
00:02:40,103 --> 00:02:43,358
to have a look around the bay which is nearby.

82
00:02:43,358 --> 00:02:44,660
It’s really beautiful.

83
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:45,181
Woman:

84
00:02:45,181 --> 00:02:48,830
Oh, I’d love to do that.

85
00:02:48,830 --> 00:02:49,188
Woman:

86
00:02:49,188 --> 00:02:53,840
Now the only time I went to Ireland it rained practically every day.

87
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,128
Jack:

88
00:02:54,128 --> 00:02:57,579
Mmm yes – that can be a problem – but you can surf in

89
00:02:57,579 --> 00:02:58,730
the rain, you know.

90
00:02:58,730 --> 00:02:59,108
Woman:

91
00:02:59,108 --> 00:03:02,130
It doesn’t have the same appeal, somehow.

92
00:03:02,130 --> 00:03:02,445
Jack:

93
00:03:02,445 --> 00:03:07,164
Well, the weather’s been fine the last couple of years when I’ve been

94
00:03:07,164 --> 00:03:07,479
there,

95
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:11,570
but actually, it tends to rain more in August than in the spring

96
00:03:11,570 --> 00:03:12,199
or autumn.

97
00:03:12,199 --> 00:03:15,660
September’s my favourite month because the water is warmer then.

98
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:15,961
Woman:

99
00:03:15,961 --> 00:03:19,570
The only problem is that the kids are back to school then.

100
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:19,967
Jack:

101
00:03:19,967 --> 00:03:20,760
I know.

102
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:26,315
But one good thing about Irish summers is that it doesn’t get too

103
00:03:26,315 --> 00:03:26,712
hot.

104
00:03:26,712 --> 00:03:32,663
The average temperature is about 19 degrees and it usually doesn’t go above 25

105
00:03:32,663 --> 00:03:33,060
degrees.

106
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:33,580
Woman:

107
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:35,140
That sounds alright.

108
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:37,220
Now what about costs?

109
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:37,577
Jack:

110
00:03:37,577 --> 00:03:42,211
Surfing is a pretty cheap holiday really – the only cost is the hire

111
00:03:42,211 --> 00:03:42,924
of equipment.

112
00:03:42,924 --> 00:03:49,342
You can expect to pay a daily rate of about 30 euros for the hire of a wetsuit

113
00:03:49,342 --> 00:03:53,977
and board – but you can save about 40 euros if you hire by

114
00:03:53,977 --> 00:03:54,690
the week.

115
00:03:54,690 --> 00:03:54,918
Woman:

116
00:03:54,918 --> 00:03:56,060
That’s not too bad.

117
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:56,393
Jack:

118
00:03:56,393 --> 00:03:56,726
No.

119
00:03:56,726 --> 00:04:01,719
It’s important to make sure you get good quality wetsuits – you’ll all get

120
00:04:01,719 --> 00:04:03,716
too cold if you don’t.

121
00:04:03,716 --> 00:04:06,047
And make sure you also get boots.

122
00:04:06,047 --> 00:04:10,707
They keep your feet warm and it’s easier to surf with them on

123
00:04:10,707 --> 00:04:11,040
too.

124
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:11,700
Woman:

125
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:12,360
OK.

126
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:15,000
Well, thanks very much …
